<title>SWITZERLAND: Ascom H1 operating profit rises 39 pct.</title>
<headline>Ascom H1 operating profit rises 39 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996:</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group operating profit     39		  vs 28</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit		 8		   vs 11</p>
<p> Group revenue		  1,403	     vs 1,398</p>
<p> Incoming orders		1,506	     vs 1,462</p>
<p> Orders on hand		 1,181	     vs 1,352</p>
<p> Net financial expense	16		  vs 27</p>
<p> Other expenses and income,</p>
<p> incl. minorities	     15 loss	   vs 10</p>
<p> Depreciation		   82		  vs 76</p>
<p> Pre-tax cash flow	    90		  vs 87</p>
<p> Capital expenditure	  56		  vs 54</p>
<p> Personnel			12,520	    vs 12,627</p>
<p> Total assets		   2,453	     vs 2,433</p>
<p> Net interest bearing debt  580		 vs 676</p>
<p> Provisions		     259		 vs 205</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is Ascom Holding AG.</p>
<p>-- Peter Nielsen, Zurich newsroom 41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
